pect it was partly  because as a writer i'd become  deeply interested in happy endings and i  thought i would try and construct one  so having constructed one there i'm i'm  now trying to construct one here and  uh again i'm grateful to president  clinton and the others at the white  house today for helping in that search  but  beyond that i can't say i think you know  you'll have to read the books and tell  me  yes i have a rather personal question  given the fact that you are the target  of uh  fundamental muslims how do you spend  your daily life  what do you do do you get ever  frustrated  oh well sure there are great  frustrations in the situation  and there and there are great  limitations on on my movements and so on  you know but  but i mean i've been trying to improve  that situation and to to reduce those  those limitations and to an extent have  succeeded  um my greatest frustration is very  simple it's that  the people that i have always drawn my  inspiration from and written about  have been given a very false impression  of the kind of writer that i am  and i have wanted very  often to try and say to them i'm not  like that i'm like this  unfortunately my voice is not loud  enough  um uh because the because i don't have  the services of  half the pulpits of half the mosques in  the world  um i find that distortion that  uh by far the most distressing aspect  of this and for a long time it used to  upset me profoundly that the book  that you know every taxi driver in cairo  would have an opinion about  the satanic verses um but that virtually  nobody would have read it  and it then occurred to me as a small  consolation that that  many of the persecutions of famous  persecutions of books  are carried out have been carried out by  people who never read the book  um it's impossible to believe that those  who  accuse joyce of of of blasphemy and  pornography and so forth had ever read  ulysses um it's it's improbable in my  mind  that um those who attacked